data_silicon_cod_9013102_teaching_snapshot
# Teaching snapshot derived from Crystallography Open Database entry 9013102.
# Source record: COD 9013102, Dutta B. N., Physica Status Solidi 2 (1962) 984-987.
# Source metadata used here: a=b=c=5.4304 Angstrom, alpha=beta=gamma=90 deg,
# diamond-cubic silicon, reported space group F d -3 m :1, T=298.15 K.
#
# IMPORTANT: this is not the byte-for-byte COD download. For stable teaching and
# visualization, the conventional diamond cell is symmetry-expanded explicitly
# and stored as P 1 with eight fully occupied Si sites.

_chemical_name_common              'Silicon'
_chemical_formula_sum              'Si'
_cell_length_a                     5.4304
_cell_length_b                     5.4304
_cell_length_c                     5.4304
_cell_angle_alpha                  90
_cell_angle_beta                   90
_cell_angle_gamma                  90
_cell_formula_units_Z              8
_diffrn_ambient_temperature        298.15
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M     'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number        1

